  "comment": "**What it does**\n**Sleep-well stocks** in the Graham defensive spirit - big, calm, financially bulletproof dividend payers. Boring on purpose.\n\n- **Big** - $10B+ only.\n- **Never-cut dividend** - a 10+ year raising streak, OR a spotless consistency record (95%+) as the fallback, so one old pause does not disqualify a good payer.\n- **Calm** - daily moves under 3%. This is your least jumpy screen by design.\n- **Bulletproof** - Altman Z in the safe zone, debt below equity, current ratio 1.2+, profitable.\n- **Sane price** - P/E under 25, so you are not buying a defensive name at a bubble multiple.\n- Debt-free companies **pass** the debt test and asset-light names **pass** Altman - those numbers are blank for them, and blank would otherwise fail.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **This screen is deliberately strict and lands around 20 names.** That scarcity is real - very few $10B+ companies are simultaneously calm, cheap, low-debt and long-raising.\n- **Biggest lever is `current_ratio`**: 1.2 gives ~20 names, 1.5 gives ~14, 1.1 gives ~22.\n- **Second lever is `pe`**: raising it from 25 to 30 jumps the list to ~34, at the cost of paying more.\n- **Want true aristocrats?** Raise `div_consecutive_years` to 25.\n- **Do not loosen `atr_pct`** - calmness is the whole point of this screen.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `quality_score`** - the thesis: durability first.\n- **Tiebreak on `income_score`** - among equally solid names, take the better payer.\n- **Avoid `growth_score`** - these are not growth names and it would rank them on an axis they are not competing on.\n- **Worth a look**: sort by `altman_z` descending to see the sturdiest balance sheets in the list.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find \"sleep well\" stocks in the Graham defensive spirit \u2014 big, calm, financially\nbulletproof dividend payers that hold up in a crash. Boring on purpose.\n- **Goal**: safety with income. **Dividends**: required, never-cut history preferred\n  (10+ year streak or a spotless consistency record).\n- **Size**: large caps, $10B and bigger. **Kinds**: normal stocks only.\n- **Calm**: low volatility \u2014 this should be my least jumpy screen.\n- **Bulletproof**: strong balance sheet (safe Altman zone, solid liquidity, debt\n  below equity). Profitable only. Valuation sane (no bubble P/E).\n- **Results**: a shortlist, ~20-100 names.\n- **Sorting**: quality first, tiebreak income.",
